{"skill":{"slug":"tavily-search-pro","displayName":"Tavily Search Pro"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770481308912,"changelog":"Tavily Search Pro 1.0.0 – Initial Release\n\n- AI-powered web search platform with 5 modes: Search, News, Finance, Extract, Crawl, Map, and Research.\n- Supports web, news, and finance search with options for LLM answers, content extraction, images, time and domain filtering.\n- Extract and summarize readable content from URLs.\n- Crawl websites, control depth, breadth, and paths.\n- Discover all URLs (sitemap) for a given site.\n- Deep research reports with citations on any topic.\n- Output options for text, markdown, or structured JSON.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":9543,"sha256":"65b4257446233997afa77ee22968bf6c9a2acdef8345848b2ee183600c90bb8a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"install.sh","size":942,"sha256":"c75ce0b9b47f43d55680754bde97e5fda8ee8fe1bf93df4e26396c6e7dd6c474","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"lib/tavily_search.py","size":19988,"sha256":"6283110343d7b4787cf55d61ad528415f8dbf13bf7cf5d52c44a8d40ef81891d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1863,"sha256":"7416eee0c0c07ab7a4f3ad49139891331161d288c195957967fcb959fc57aece","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789038474396,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"c7c4bf1cfd831ddde7848cb7b9b045fa95b44e0c8f68cc907510eced4ea635e3","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/c7c4bf1cfd831ddde7848cb7b9b045fa95b44e0c8f68cc907510eced4ea635e3","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: tavily-search-pro\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is designed to interact with the Tavily AI search platform. It requires the `TAVILY_API_KEY` environment variable, which is read by the Python script `lib/tavily_search.py`. The `install.sh` script handles standard Python dependency installation via `pip` and performs a benign smoke test. The core Python script makes HTTP POST requests exclusively to `https://api.tavily.com`, which is the legitimate API endpoint for Tavily. There is no evidence of data exfiltration to unauthorized endpoints, malicious execution of arbitrary code, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent. The use of `exec` is limited to running the provided Python script, which is necessary for its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162074294},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":63,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":4,"checkedAt":1789038474396},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"medium","summary":"This Tavily search skill appears purpose-aligned, but it sends user queries and URLs to an external API and installs an unpinned dependency into the shared Python environment.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The required TAVILY_API_KEY and outbound Tavily API use are coherent for this integration, but the declared metadata only lists the environment variable and pip package, not a scoped network destination or privacy boundary.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"install.sh installs the unpinned tavily-python package and first tries pip with --break-system-packages, which can modify a shared system Python environment and pulls mutable upstream code at install time.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"External Tavily processing is central to the skill, but SKILL.md does not clearly warn users that submitted queries, URLs, internal targets, and crawl/research parameters leave the local environment.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"I found no artifact evidence of persistence, background workers, credential harvesting, tool spoofing, destructive actions, or local file indexing beyond reading the Tavily API key from the environment.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill's search, extract, crawl, map, and research features match its stated Tavily web-search purpose, and the code posts user-supplied queries, URLs, crawl instructions, and options to https://api.tavily.com.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this before installing if you may search confidential topics or internal URLs: those inputs are sent to Tavily's external service. Prefer using it only with non-sensitive queries, and install the dependency in an isolated virtual environment with a pinned version rather than running the provided system-level pip install path.","findings":"[LP1] expected: Outbound requests to api.tavily.com are expected for a Tavily-backed search skill, but the artifact does not declare a scoped network permission or clearly describe the off-platform data flow.\n[SQP-2] expected: Sending queries, URLs, crawl targets, and research inputs to Tavily is purpose-aligned, but the user-facing instructions lack a prominent privacy warning for sensitive prompts or internal URLs.\n[T08] expected: The tavily-python dependency is relevant to the skill, but the installer uses an unpinned package and --break-system-packages, making the installation broader and less reproducible than needed.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789038474396}}}}}